# Meta-Linguistic Correction Plan (The Fix)

Now that we know exactly why the audio pipeline is eating itself alive, here is a surgical plan to patch the translation and synthesis engines so they operate flawlessly within physical constraints.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [transcribe.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/transcribe.py)
**Objective**: Fix the "Spanglish" Hallucination.
- Remove the `language="en"` parameter completely. This frees the model to listen natively to Mandarin (or any language).
- Swap the task from `task="transcribe"` to `task="translate"`. This forces Faster-Whisper to correctly process the foreign language and output a raw English string under the hood, completely eradicating the phonetic word-salad that was confusing the LLM.

### [MODIFY] [translate.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/translate.py)
**Objective**: Fix the Verbose Audio Distortions.
- Remove the vague *"Target Duration"* prompt. LLMs do not understand time. They only understand tokens/words.
- Implement a physical constraint algorithm: `Max_Words = max(2, int(duration_seconds * 2.5))` (Since average English speech is ~2.5 words per second).
- Inject a strict limit into the prompt: *"Constraint: Your translation MUST NOT exceed {Max_Words} words. Do not ignore this limit."* This guarantees the LLM will output a tiny sentence for a tiny timeframe.

### [MODIFY] [audio_mix.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/audio_mix.py)
**Objective**: Muzzle the ATempo "Chipmunk" Distortion.
- Put a maximum cap on the time-stretcher. If the required speed exceeds 1.5x, we cap it at 1.5x and simply trim any overflowing audio. This prevents the Mixer from shrinking 5 seconds of audio into 0.5s, avoiding ear-piercing chipmunk squeaks.

## User Review Required
> [!WARNING]
> Implementing these fixes requires us to **start completely from scratch**. We will need to purge the entire workspace (including the original whisper transcriptions, translations, and TTS). 
> Because the foundation itself (the raw transcription) is currently polluted with word-salad and missing data, we cannot reuse anything. 

